Z||000000||John E. Rowlett||07-06-2001||02:02 PM||||Hey Folks.  My right headlight goes up just fine but will not go down. Does this mean that the nylon gear is bad or what? <BR>Thanks John R.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||84Bill||07-06-2001||02:11 PM||||Hi John, Welcome to the Forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I would guess that you switch might be bad, Try  giving the button a wiggle or or two while in the off position.<BR>If the gears are bad you will hear it clunking quite a bit in the full up or down position.<P>There are 4 relays in the front (depending on the year 87 & 88 are different) located on the headlight mounting brackets. Give them a tap while someone pushes the light switch off.||||reg||14
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||07-06-2001||02:13 PM||||Yep.... if it keeps making that running sound, it probably is.  If you're enterprising and lucky, you may be able to remove the gear and reinstall so that the portion not normally used engages.<BR>Welcome to the Forum<BR>Gary||||reg||1
